---
source: crates/cli/tests/lint.rs
expression: out(&one)
---
sorted-keys
  languages:     all
  category:      style
  default level: off
  fix:           unsafe
  equivalent:    Biome assist/source/useSortedKeys (partial), eslint-plugin-jsonc jsonc/sort-keys (partial), taplo reorder_keys (partial), taplo reorder_inline_tables (partial), yamllint key-ordering (partial), yamllint key-ordering.ignored-keys

The keys of a mapping are not in order (alphabetical by default). The keys reported are chosen by `report`, and the first report carries the fix. Comments on lines of their own stay where they are, a comment after an entry moves with it; moving a YAML anchor below its alias breaks the document, so the fix is unsafe.

Options:
  order (a list of strings, default []): Keys that come first, in this order; the rest follow in the configured order.
  direction (a string, default "asc"): `asc` or `desc`.
  compare (a string, default "ordinal"): `ordinal` (code points), `case_insensitive`, or `natural` (digit runs compare as numbers: `a2` before `a10`).
  ignored_keys (a list of strings, default []): Regular expressions; matching keys stay where they are and are not compared.
  min_keys (an integer, default 2): Mappings with fewer keys are not checked.
  blank_line_groups (a boolean, default false): Sort each run of entries between blank lines on its own.
  report (a string, default "moved"): Which keys are reported. `moved`: the fewest keys that would have to move (eslint-plugin-jsonc). `misplaced`: every key that sorts before one above it (yamllint).

Example:
  { "b": 1, "a": 2 }   // becomes { "a": 2, "b": 1 }
